      },
      "text": "2 January – Rio de Janeiro to Lima"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b9ad3e14216c2f08",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "a010c4314e75bf38d69604e723755dbbdbecfa1d7f5f5ced37a106b5270303b0",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "submit-9e9cff89-eaf8-4da3-b719-163cca50324d-10",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "Have breakfast at the hotel, then transfer to the airport for your flight to Lima. On arrival, an English-speaking guide will meet you for the transfer to **Belmond Miraflores Park**, where you’ll stay in a **Junior Suite**.\n\nAfter check-in, set out on a sightseeing tour of Lima. Spanish colonists founded the city in 1535, and it was known as the City of Kings. Cathedrals, mansions for the Spanish nobility and the viceroy’s palace were built here. The colonial architecture survives today.\n\nLima sits on the Pacific coast at the foot of the Andes. Your tour starts in Miraflores at the Park of Love. From there, see the Olive Grove Park and the colonial estates of San Isidro, then take in a panoramic view of the Huaca Pucllana pyramid, which dates back about 2,500 years.\n\nIn the Plaza de Armas, you’ll see City Hall, the Government Palace and the Cathedral, which houses the tomb of Francisco Pizarro."
    }
